{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_even(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a new list as a shallow copy to preserve odd indexed values and ensure O(n) memory usage.\n    l_prime = list(l)\n\n    # Extract values from even indices for sorting.\n    even_values = [l[i] for i in range(len(l)) if i % 2 == 0]\n\n    # Sort the extracted even values in ascending order.\n    even_values.sort()\n\n    # Re-insert the sorted even values back into the new list at their original even positions.\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    for i in range(len(l_prime)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            l_prime[i] = even_values[sorted_idx]\n            sorted_idx += 1\n\n    return l_prime\n```"}
