{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 sequence iteratively.\n    Initializes base values and calculates subsequent terms using a dynamic programming approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # As per instructions, trust input; this case shouldn't occur for typical fib4 definitions.\n        # However, for direct array access with negative indices, it would error or wrap around.\n        # Assuming n will be non-negative.\n        pass\n\n    # Initialize a list with the base values as specified.\n    fib_sequence = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Handle base cases directly.\n    if n < len(fib_sequence):\n        return fib_sequence[n]\n\n    # Iterate from 4 up to n, calculating each fib4(i).\n    for i in range(len(fib_sequence), n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_sequence[i-1] + fib_sequence[i-2] + fib_sequence[i-3] + fib_sequence[i-4]\n        fib_sequence.append(next_fib)\n\n    # Return the last computed value, which is fib4(n).\n    return fib_sequence[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2"}
