{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes 2^n modulo p using modular exponentiation.\n    This method efficiently handles large exponents by reducing intermediate results modulo p.\n    \"\"\"\n    res = 1\n    base = 2\n\n    # Ensure the base is within the modulo range from the start.\n    base %= p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        # If n is odd, multiply the current result by the base and take modulo p.\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            res = (res * base) % p\n\n        # Square the base and take modulo p for the next iteration.\n        base = (base * base) % p\n\n        # Halve the exponent n.\n        n //= 2\n\n    return res"}
