{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string by reversing a 5-character shift in the alphabet.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        # 1. Get ASCII value\n        # 2. Subtract 'a' ASCII for 0-indexed position\n        # 3. Subtract 5 to shift back\n        # 4. Apply modulo 26 for wrap-around\n        # 5. Add 'a' ASCII back for decoded character ASCII\n        # 6. Convert ASCII to character\n        decoded_char_ascii = ((ord(ch) - ord('a') - 5) % 26) + ord('a')\n        decoded_chars.append(chr(decoded_char_ascii))\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
