{"task_id": "HumanEval/68", "solution": "def pluck(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest even value and its index in an array.\n    Returns an empty list if no even values or the array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    smallest_even_value = float('inf')\n    smallest_even_index = -1\n\n    for index, value in enumerate(arr):\n        if value % 2 == 0:  # Check if the value is even\n            if value < smallest_even_value:\n                smallest_even_value = value\n                smallest_even_index = index\n            # If value is equal to smallest_even_value, we keep the earlier encountered index\n            # as it will naturally have the smaller index due to left-to-right iteration.\n\n    if smallest_even_index == -1:\n        return []\n    else:\n        return [smallest_even_value, smallest_even_index]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/68", "solution": "```python\ndef pluck(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest even number in `arr` and returns it with its first index `[value, index]`.\n    Returns `[]` if `arr` is empty or contains no even numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    smallest_even_value = None\n    smallest_even_index = -1\n\n    for i, num in enumerate(arr):\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            if smallest_even_value is None or num < smallest_even_value:\n                smallest_even_value = num\n                smallest_even_index = i\n            # If num == smallest_even_value, we do not update, preserving the smallest index.\n\n    if smallest_even_value is not None:\n        return [smallest_even_value, smallest_even_index]\n    else:\n        return []\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/70", "solution": "def strange_sort_list(lst):\n    '''\n    Given list of integers, return list in strange order.\n    Strange sorting, is when you start with the minimum value,\n    then maximum of the remaining integers, then minimum and so on.\n\n    Examples:\n    strange_sort_list([1, 2, 3, 4]) == [1, 4, 2, 3]\n    strange_sort_list([5, 5, 5, 5]) == [5, 5, 5, 5]\n    strange_sort_list([]) == []\n    '''\n    result = []\n    current_list = sorted(list(lst))\n    is_min_turn = True\n\n    while current_list:\n        if is_min_turn:\n            result.append(current_list.pop(0))\n        else:\n            result.append(current_list.pop())\n        is_min_turn = not is_min_turn\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/69", "solution": "```python\ndef search(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the greatest integer N in the list whose frequency is greater than or equal to N.\n    Returns -1 if no such integer exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    frequency_map = {}\n\n    # Count frequencies of each number in the list.\n    for num in lst:\n        frequency_map[num] = frequency_map.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    # Get unique numbers and sort them in descending order.\n    unique_numbers = list(frequency_map.keys())\n    unique_numbers.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    # Iterate through sorted unique numbers to find the greatest satisfying one.\n    for num in unique_numbers:\n        if frequency_map[num] >= num:\n            return num\n\n    # If no such number is found after checking all unique numbers.\n    return -1\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "```python\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return the area of\n    the triangle rounded to 2 decimal points if the three sides form a valid triangle.\n    Otherwise return -1\n    '''\n    # Input Validation: Check if sides are positive and satisfy triangle inequality\n    if not (a > 0 and b > 0 and c > 0 and a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n\n    # Calculate area using Heron's formula\n    area = (s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)) ** 0.5\n\n    # Round the area to 2 decimal places\n    return round(area, 2)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/70", "solution": "```python\ndef strange_sort_list(lst):\n    '''\n    Sorts a list of integers in a peculiar way, alternating between minimum and maximum remaining values.\n    Handles an empty list by returning an empty list.\n    '''\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    sorted_lst = sorted(lst)\n    result = []\n    left = 0\n    right = len(sorted_lst) - 1\n    is_min_turn = True\n\n    while left <= right:\n        if is_min_turn:\n            result.append(sorted_lst[left])\n            left += 1\n        else:\n            result.append(sorted_lst[right])\n            right -= 1\n        is_min_turn = not is_min_turn\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return the area of\n    the triangle rounded to 2 decimal points if the three sides form a valid triangle.\n    Otherwise return -1\n    '''\n    # Validate if the sides form a valid triangle using the Triangle Inequality Theorem.\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate the semi-perimeter (s).\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n\n    # Calculate the area using Heron's formula.\n    area = math.sqrt(s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c))\n\n    # Round the calculated area to 2 decimal points.\n    return round(area, 2)\n```"}
